-- Layer A (pre-attempt) + Layer C (generic failure) hints for the 96 slice-1 signs.
-- Authored mechanically from ASL-LEX 2.0 phonological data (Sevcikova Sehyr et al. 2021).
-- Slice-1 only per ADR 0004; slice-2 production-deployment work replaces with
-- Deaf-signer-reviewed copy. Re-run is idempotent (UPDATEs in place).

update public.vocabulary_items set pre_attempt_hint = 'Before signing NICE, set up: the documented handshape (see reference), on the non-dominant hand, the hand moves in a straight line. This is a two-handed sign.', generic_failure_hint = 'Common failure: the non-dominant hand drops position or rotates; keep it steady. Common failure: the movement is cut short; let the full motion complete. Common failure: missing the contact point; the hand should actually touch the indicated location. If unsure, watch the reference and check: handshape, palm orientation, location, movement, facial expression.' where id = 'nice';
